 ## Overview
-Hard Voxelization (Deterministic) converts a 3D point cloud into a fixed-size voxel grid by assigning each point to a discrete voxel based on its coordinates and a specified voxel size and range [S2, unofficial]. It handles duplicate points within the same voxel and limits the number of points per voxel and total voxels [S2, unofficial]. Unlike the non-deterministic variant which uses atomic operations for speed at the cost of reproducibility, this method guarantees bit-identical output by using stable sorting and explicit ordering logic [S2, unofficial]. It builds on [Hard Voxelization](5345-hard-voxelization.md).
